by HypeMC at 2026-04-13T23:45:04Z

@GromNaN The `#[MapEntity]` attribute already supports loading lists of entities via [an expression](https://symfony.com/doc/current/doctrine.html#fetch-via-an-expression):

```php
#[Route('/posts_by/{author_id}')]
public function authorPosts(
    #[MapEntity(class: Post::class, expr: 'repository.findBy({"author": author_id}, {}, 10)')]
    iterable $posts
): Response {
}
```

So adding a new attribute might not be necessary. As for the `$limit`, `$offset`, and `$orderBy` options, this can already be achieved via an expression, or via a closure if #63866 gets accepted.

